; BG_SKY over a GOLD sky with AMBIENT_SOURCE_COLOR (flat 0.6,
; ambient_light_sky_contribution = 0) and AgX tonemapping. The gold sky lets two
; things separate by colour:
;   * the shadowed grass, lit only by the flat grey ambient, must stay grey —
;     a warm tint means sky IBL is leaking into diffuse despite contribution 0;
;   * the metallic sphere, reflecting the sky, must read GOLD — a grey/black
;     sphere means the reflection was switched off with the ambient.
